+# Aegis — Acceptance Drills & Runbooks
+
+This document lists the acceptance drills to run before declaring Aegis production Level‑4 for a pilot.
+
+1) Milvus backup & restore drill
+ - Precondition: backups configured and recent successful backup exists.
+ - Steps:
+   a) Run services/milvus/restore_drill.sh (ensure maintenance window).
+   b) Verify collection data and sample queries return expected results.
+   c) Record restore time (RTO) and integrity checksums.
+
+2) Webhook fail‑open / fail‑closed test
+ - Precondition: ValidatingWebhookConfiguration created with failurePolicy set to Ignore (fail-open) for staging.
+ - Steps:
+   a) Simulate webhook outage (scale webhook deployment to 0).
+   b) Observe behavior: with failurePolicy Ignore, API server allows requests; with Fail, requests are blocked.
+   c) Toggle failurePolicy and document operational decision.
+
+3) HIL evidence run & FMEA sign‑off
+ - Steps:
+   a) Execute an HIL scenario in lab that generates HIL evidence bundle.
+   b) Use receipt_signer to sign evidence and create FMEA entry.
+   c) Ensure HIL gate blocks promotion when evidence missing; verify acceptance when evidence present.
+
+4) Fetchtoken redemption audit (edge)
+ - Precondition: fetchtokens provisioned and offline fallback deployed on edge.
+ - Steps:
+   a) Redeem a fetchtoken on offline node using services/edge/offline_a2a_fallback.py endpoint.
+   b) Verify a local approval record is created and later synced to MCP when connectivity returns.
+   c) Review audit entry in MCP for token use.
+
+5) Key rotation & secret rotation rehearsal
+ - Steps:
+   a) Use services/security/key_rotation.py or Vault rotation workflow to rotate a public key/secret.
+   b) Patch deployments to reference new secret, validate rollout, and delete old secret.
+   c) Document rollback steps.
+
+Record results and any remediation. Only flip Gatekeeper constraints to "deny" after drills succeed and CI evidence indicates artifacts are signed.
+
