+# Aegis — Production Infra & Hardening Quick Guide
+
+This unified patch includes helpers and manifests to:
+- Provision placeholder Kubernetes secrets & configmaps (infra/k8s/provision_core.sh).
+- CI workflow to build/push images and cosign + Rekor attestations (ci/build_and_sign_and_push.yml).
+- Gatekeeper audit tips and webhook deployment sample with HA Deployment + ValidatingWebhookConfiguration (k8s/webhooks/*).
+- Node labeling helper for kata and PREEMPT_RT pools (infra/nodepool_labeling.sh).
+- CI check to verify cosign signatures on images referenced in k8s manifests (ci/cosign_rekor_policy.yml).
+- Monitoring alerts and Grafana dashboard examples (k8s/monitoring/*, grafana/*).
+- Milvus restore drill helper and acceptance drills runbook (services/milvus/restore_drill.sh, docs/acceptance_drills.md).
+- Vault integration helper and key rotation pattern (services/security/*).
+
+Operator checklist (high level):
+1. Provision cloud resources (KMS, S3/MinIO, Rekor, registry, Postgres) via IaC.
+2. Replace placeholders in infra/k8s/provision_core.sh and run it to create base k8s secrets/configmaps.
+3. Configure and run CI (update repo secrets used by ci/build_and_sign_and_push.yml).
+4. Deploy Gatekeeper + webhook in audit mode; collect violations for 48–72h and remediate.
+5. Execute acceptance drills in docs/acceptance_drills.md. Fix issues and iterate.
+6. Flip Gatekeeper constraints to enforce (deny) only after CI + webhooks + signing + Rekor are validated.
+
+Security notes:
+- Do not store production private keys in repo or plain Kubernetes secrets; use Vault or cloud KMS.
+- Use least-privilege service accounts for Argo/MLflow/training jobs.
+
